# AYSO Region 13

> AYSO Region 13 is a 501(c)(3) nonprofit youth soccer organization providing volunteer-run programs for players ages 4-19 in Pasadena, Altadena, La Canada Flintridge, and surrounding communities. Founded in {{ site.founded }}. Phone: {{ site.phone }}. Address: {{ site.address }}, {{ site.city }}.

AYSO Region 13 is affiliated with AYSO National (American Youth Soccer Organization). Core philosophies: Everyone Plays (minimum 50% playing time), Balanced Teams, Open Registration (no tryouts), Positive Coaching, Good Sportsmanship, and Player Development.

## Programs

- [Fall Soccer (6U-14U)]({{ site.url }}/programs/fall-soccer/): The core recreational program. Saturday games September through mid-November. {{ fees.fall.rangeShort }}.
- [Spring Soccer (6U-19U)]({{ site.url }}/programs/spring-soccer/): March-May Interlock season; recreational for 6U-14U and competitive Spring Cup for 16U-19U.
- [Upper Division (16U/19U)]({{ site.url }}/programs/upper-division/): High-school-age soccer; schedules avoid conflicts with school teams.
- [Preschool (4U/5U)]({{ site.url }}/programs/preschool/): Introductory soccer for ages 3-5.
- [NEXT]({{ site.url }}/programs/next/): Advanced training program for skilled 10U-14U players.
- [All-Stars]({{ site.url }}/programs/all-stars/): Competitive winter program; teams represent Region 13 in tournaments against other AYSO regions.
- [EXTRA™]({{ site.url }}/programs/extra/): Tryout-based select program for 10U launching Fall 2026; competes against other EXTRA teams in Section 1 West, Fall through Spring.
- [Winter Stars]({{ site.url }}/programs/winter-stars/): Skills training and small-sided games for returning fall players, December-February.
- [Grad Series]({{ site.url }}/programs/grad-series/): 8-week winter program helping 8U graduates transition to 10U format.
- [EPIC]({{ site.url }}/programs/epic/): Adaptive soccer program pairing players who need field assistance with volunteer buddies. EPIC fee {{ fees.epic }}.

